<urn:atm:triage:finding/BB7-TEMPLATE-CONTRADICTION-001>
  a triage:Finding ;
  triage:findingId "BB7-TEMPLATE-CONTRADICTION-001" ;
  triage:title "Live dispatch templates and team-protocol.md still tell every assignee to atm ack and never atm task start, contradicting BB.4/BB.5's shipped behavior" ;
  triage:description "req-qa (NEW-BB-QA-002), independently confirmed by quality-mgr (2026-09-13T04:35:38Z), during BB-POST-MORTEM-1789304000 phase-ending gate against integrate/phase-bb @ 4b1bf0e63. Direct consequence of BB7-DOCS-NONDELIVERY-001 (BB.7 D1/D4 never landed). The six live orchestration dispatch templates (.claude/skills/graph-orchestration/{dev-task,dev-fix}.xml.j2; .claude/skills/codex-orchestration/{dev-template,fix-assignment,review-template,qa-template}.xml.j2) still instruct every assignee to `atm ack` the assignment first and never `atm task start`. docs/team-protocol.md:61-66 still classes 'task assignment' under requires_ack. But BB.4 already shipped `atm task start` as the only assigned->active transition (the daemon no longer starts tasks), and BB.5 already shipped requires_ack = false for assignments. Once this phase merges to develop, the templates this team actually uses to dispatch all dev/QA work will tell every assignee to do the wrong thing (ack, no longer required) and never do the now-required thing (atm task start) -- defeating the phase's own stated goal ('task transitions you can see') and failing phase acceptance criterion Sec9 item 8 verbatim." ;
  triage:phaseId "phase-bb" ;
  triage:triageMode "initial_pass" ;
  triage:category "correctness" ;
  triage:severity "blocking" ;
  triage:source "req-qa, verified by quality-mgr, BB-POST-MORTEM-1789304000 phase-ending gate" ;
  triage:repeatable true ;
  triage:sweepScope "docs/team-protocol.md:54-80; .claude/skills/graph-orchestration/{dev-task,dev-fix}.xml.j2; .claude/skills/codex-orchestration/{dev-template,fix-assignment,review-template,qa-template}.xml.j2; both SKILL.md dispatch sections; ~/.atm/templates/codex-orchestration/ host-only variants (reported with diff, not edited, per BB.2 D4 rule)" ;
  triage:status "open" ;
  triage:dispatchReady true ;
  triage:triagedAt "2026-09-13T04:35:38Z"^^xsd:dateTime ;
  triage:deferredNote "Lead ruling (2026-09-13, team-lead): blocking, confirmed -- do not merge to develop with the live dispatch templates telling every assignee the wrong protocol. Resolved by BB.7 D1/D3/D4 exactly as scoped in sprint-BB.7-docs.md (team-protocol.md rewrite, agent-conventions.md task-lines section, ack step deleted from all six templates + replaced with `atm task start {{ task_id }} \"...\"` as step one). Dispatched to cipher together with BB7-DOCS-NONDELIVERY-001 as one BB.7 fix layer, not a separate branch -- they are the same sprint's deliverables. UPDATE (2026-09-13T05:19:57Z): quality-mgr BB7-DOCS-QA1-1789320500 (report 01M2CKA77FGJHZ9E1M0QY55MYV, PR #1478) confirms D1/D4's core edits landed but 3 occurrences of the same defect class were missed by the sprint's file scope -- correlated below as occurrences 2-4 rather than filed as new records. STAYS OPEN. Fix round BB7-DOCS-FIX-R1-1789329000 dispatched to cipher on the same branch (feature/bb7-docs); re-verification follows on his final SHA. ATM-QA-BB7-004 (minor, host-only ~/.atm/templates/codex-orchestration/dev-template-cipher/solar.xml.j2 still ack-first) is fenix's own post-merge host-sync item, not tracked as a separate triage record. UPDATE (2026-09-13T05:43:56Z): quality-mgr BB7-DOCS-QA2-1789332000 (PR #1478, round 2) confirms occurrences 1-4 genuinely fixed by cipher's BB7-DOCS-FIX-R1-1789329000 push (feature/bb7-docs @ 9167bd479, compose_passthrough re-verified 3/3) -- closed below. But req-qa's mandated sweep found 2 NEW live occurrences of the same task-linked-ack defect class (ATM-QA-BB7-101/102), personally verified by quality-mgr via git show at 84ea982ee -- correlated below as occurrences 5-6 rather than filed as new records. STAYS OPEN pending next fix layer. UPDATE (2026-09-13T05:46:26Z): fenix's own broad sweep at the same head (84ea982ee) found 7 more live instances of the same defect class -- correlated below as occurrences 7-15 rather than filed as new records: .claude/agents/quality-mgr.md:145,272,308; .claude/skills/publishing/SKILL.md:54; .claude/skills/publishing/preflight.xml.j2:41; .claude/skills/publishing/publish.xml.j2:39; CLAUDE.md:81 ('ack -> work -> task close'); .claude/skills/quality-management-gh/SKILL.md:164; .claude/skills/triaging-findings/SKILL.md:379 ('ack, work, task close'). Fix round BB7-DOCS-FIX-R2-1789333000 dispatched to cipher on the same branch (closed hit list). STAYS OPEN pending re-verification. UPDATE (2026-09-13T05:57:17Z): fenix found one more live instance at feature/bb7-docs @ 37d06b1ec after cipher's R2 push -- docs/team-protocol.md:127 ('If blocked, send an immediate ack plus blocker status') -- correlated below as occurrence 16, addendum sent to cipher on the same branch. Occurrences 5-15 reported fixed by cipher at 37d06b1ec; awaiting the round-3 QA verdict before closing anything. STAYS OPEN. UPDATE (2026-09-13T06:10:25Z): quality-mgr BB7-DOCS-QA3 (PR #1478, round 3) confirms occurrences 5-16 genuinely fixed at feature/bb7-docs @ caf73bc34 (compose_passthrough 3/3, doc lint gate green, confirmed independently by req-qa and arch-qa) -- closed below. But the mandated ack/acknowledg sweep found 8 more live instances of the same defect class (7 in Mandatory Baseline Sources docs + 1 live skill nudge payload), personally verified by quality-mgr via git show at caf73bc34 -- correlated below as occurrences 17-24 rather than filed as new records. quality-mgr recommends one full-corpus grep for this pattern before round 4, since it has resurfaced across 3 rounds. STAYS OPEN pending round 4." ;
  triage:foundIn triage:BB7 ;
  triage:foundAt "2026-09-13T04:35:38Z"^^xsd:dateTime ;
